[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked **known: one issue, one fix queued**. Its own data says
otherwise. The reports merged into it share a subject ("wrong day", "dates mixed up"), because
[decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. They do not share a
cause. Sorted by what actually went wrong, #4471 holds three problems, and each now has a ticket of
its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the <code>parser</code> problem. The <code>hint</code> and
<code>one-day</code> reports will keep coming after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## How each report was placed

1. **One id, one report.** The ticket export comes in overlapping pages, so some reports appear
   twice. Count unique ids (`uniqueById`), never rows.
2. **The tenant decides, not intake.** The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. The
   cause comes from the tenant: its locale (day first or not) and its booking form (`causes.ts`).
   Intake's tags disagree with the tenant's cause in both directions; the table shows by how much.
3. **Read the outliers.** A few reports are not a day-month swap at all: the month stays, the day
   moves by one ("Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday", "every booking in June is one day off").
   The desk already noted them (`desk-notes.json → oneDayMove`) but filed them under `parser` by
   tenant. They are their own problem: time zones, not date order.

## The three problems

- **`parser`**: the shared date parser reads every date month first. Every day-first tenant is hit,
  through every channel. This is the fix #4471 already has queued.
- **`hint`**: `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at day-first tenants
  type what the hint says, and the form reads it day first. Only form reports from `booking-v3`
  tenants. Fix the hint (or the form's reading), not the parser.
- **`one-day`**: the date keeps its month and slides by a day between what was booked and what the
  invite shows, and differs by where the invitee is. A time-zone / DST conversion bug.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## What the desk should change

- Re-open #4471 as the `parser` ticket only, and link the two new tickets from it.
- Merge on cause, not subject: two reports with the same subject can have different causes, and two
  with different subjects the same one (see [triage](/kb/triage/dedupe), *Try it*). Decision 0001 is
  accepted and stays as written; replacing it needs a new decision record.
- When a big ticket's table shows more than one row, it is more than one ticket.

